WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.585
Let's make A summer nature mandala.

2
00:00:02.965 --> 00:00:06.930
Arrange loose leaves, petals and stones in repeating circles.

3
00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:10.725
This is a temporary picture you can change as you go.

4
00:00:11.105 --> 00:00:13.185
Make this project with a grown-up.

5
00:00:13.565 --> 00:00:16.295
Gather the supplies listed below the video.

6
00:00:16.675 --> 00:00:18.920
Pause whenever you need more time.

7
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.575
An adult checks plants and stones.

8
00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:26.640
Collect only permitted loose materials; take every added piece away when finished.

9
00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:29.357
Step 1.

10
00:00:29.737 --> 00:00:31.602
Sort your summer finds.

11
00:00:31.982 --> 00:00:36.242
Sort leaves, petals and stones into three groups beside the tray.

12
00:00:36.622 --> 00:00:38.607
Pair pieces that look similar.

13
00:00:38.987 --> 00:00:41.832
Keep the middle of the tray empty for the design.

14
00:00:42.212 --> 00:00:43.592
Grown-up help.

15
00:00:43.972 --> 00:00:46.277
Check all plant pieces and stones.

16
00:00:47.667 --> 00:00:48.847
Step 2.

17
00:00:49.227 --> 00:00:50.602
Choose a centre.

18
00:00:50.982 --> 00:00:53.372
Put one stone in the middle of the tray.

19
00:00:53.752 --> 00:00:58.577
Place four leaves around it like compass points, with tips facing outward.

20
00:00:58.957 --> 00:01:01.237
Leave small gaps between them.

21
00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:04.012
Step 3.

22
00:01:04.392 --> 00:01:05.997
Complete the inner ring.

23
00:01:06.377 --> 00:01:10.612
Place the remaining four leaves in the spaces between the first leaves.

24
00:01:10.992 --> 00:01:12.432
Turn each tip outward.

25
00:01:12.812 --> 00:01:15.662
Move the leaves until the ring looks balanced.

26
00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:18.317
Step 4.

27
00:01:18.697 --> 00:01:19.872
Repeat outward.

28
00:01:20.252 --> 00:01:23.237
Arrange the eight remaining stones in a wider ring.

29
00:01:23.617 --> 00:01:26.722
Place petals in pairs or small groups in the gaps.

30
00:01:27.102 --> 00:01:30.647
Leave room between the rings so the shapes are easy to see.

31
00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:33.342
Step 5.

32
00:01:33.722 --> 00:01:34.997
Look from above.

33
00:01:35.377 --> 00:01:37.722
Step back or look straight down.

34
00:01:38.102 --> 00:01:41.882
Adjust one piece at a time, give the pattern a name and remember it

35
00:01:41.882 --> 00:01:43.232
with a photo or drawing.

36
00:01:43.612 --> 00:01:45.437
Then gather every piece.

37
00:01:45.817 --> 00:01:47.197
Grown-up help.

38
00:01:47.577 --> 00:01:49.972
Supervise collection and cleanup.

39
00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:54.415
Here are three ideas for your finished project.

40
00:01:54.795 --> 00:01:58.345
These example pictures were made with artificial intelligence.

41
00:01:58.725 --> 00:02:00.745
Your creation can look different.

42
00:02:01.125 --> 00:02:06.049
Reuse the tray and return or dispose of suitable natural pieces according to local

43
00:02:06.049 --> 00:02:06.400
rules.

44
00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:10.585
Photograph or draw the temporary arrangement before dismantling it.

45
00:02:10.965 --> 00:02:11.955
Well done.

46
00:02:12.335 --> 00:02:14.765
Take a moment to enjoy what you made.

